From: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cam_mem_mgr: guard krefcount put against underflow on abnormal close

On cam-server abnormal exit the v4l2 fd release runs cam_req_mgr_close ->
cam_mem_mgr_deinit -> cam_mem_mgr_close(), which calls __cam_mem_mgr_release()
for every still-active buffer and kref_put()s its krefcount.

cam_mem_put_cpu_buf() releases the kernel-side krefcount with the no-op
cam_mem_util_unmap_dummy release. When that drops krefcount to 0 while
userspace still holds the buffer (urefcount > 0) it cannot unmap, hits the
"Unbalanced release" case and leaves the buffer active with krefcount == 0.
cam_mem_mgr_close() then puts that krefcount a second time.

On the downstream vendor kernel the extra put wrapped silently; on a mainline
(linux-yocto) kernel refcount_t is strict, so it is a use-after-free:

  refcount_t: underflow; use-after-free.
  WARNING ... refcount_warn_saturate
   cam_mem_mgr_deinit [camera_qcm6490]
   cam_req_mgr_close [camera_qcm6490]
   v4l2_release -> __fput -> do_exit -> get_signal

It also leaves the mem manager in a bad state so the next camera open fails
("mem_mgr not initialized" -> ICP FW download failed) until a later retry.

Skip the put when krefcount is already 0. cam_mem_mgr_cleanup_table(), run
right after cam_mem_mgr_close() in cam_mem_mgr_deinit(), still force-frees any
buffer left active (unmap + dma_buf_put), so nothing leaks.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [adapts downstream camx-dlkm to a mainline kernel]

---
diff --git a/camera_kt/drivers/cam_req_mgr/cam_mem_mgr.c b/camera_kt/drivers/cam_req_mgr/cam_mem_mgr.c
index 5e057c1..ece482a 100644
--- a/camera_kt/drivers/cam_req_mgr/cam_mem_mgr.c
+++ b/camera_kt/drivers/cam_req_mgr/cam_mem_mgr.c
@@ -1368,6 +1368,17 @@ static int __cam_mem_mgr_release(struct cam_mem_mgr_release_cmd *cmd)
 	}
 
 	CAM_DBG(CAM_MEM, "Releasing hdl = %x, idx = %d", cmd->buf_handle, idx);
+	/*
+	 * A prior unbalanced put (cam_mem_put_cpu_buf) can leave a buffer active with
+	 * krefcount already 0; putting again here underflows refcount_t (UAF) on mainline.
+	 * Skip it - cleanup_table() (next in deinit) still force-frees the buffer.
+	 */
+	if (!kref_read(&tbl.bufq[idx].krefcount)) {
+		CAM_WARN(CAM_MEM,
+			"krefcount already 0 for buf_handle %u idx %d; skip put to avoid underflow",
+			cmd->buf_handle, idx);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
 	if (kref_put(&tbl.bufq[idx].krefcount, cam_mem_util_unmap_dummy)) {
 		CAM_DBG(CAM_MEM,
 			"Called unmap from here, buf_handle: %u, idx: %d",
